<!--
  The adaptive icon's foreground layer — and its monochrome layer, and the splash
  screen's icon. The mark is a flat silhouette, so the themed-icon tint has nothing to
  strip out of it, and the splash shows the middle two thirds of its canvas exactly as
  the launcher mask does, so one layer serves all three.

  The mark is a family group over the connector the app draws its own diagram with — a
  stem, a sibling bar and three nodes — so the icon says "family tree" rather than
  "contacts". The figures come from the icon in ~/Downloads/family-insurance-icon.svg;
  the cupped hands that came with them were dropped, being thin outlines that fill in to
  a white blob at 48dp.

  Everything sits inside the 66dp safe circle, which is why the artwork looks small
  against the 108dp canvas: the launcher crops this layer to 72dp and any mask it likes
  within that, and a round mask is the tightest of them. The scale below is the largest
  one that survives it — measured, not guessed.
-->
